      "excerpt_text": "NIH ODS explains that vitamin C supplements come in multiple forms (e.g., ascorbic acid, sodium/calcium ascorbate, and combination products such as Ester‑C). It reports that some human studies found similar plasma vitamin C across forms, and that authors concluded simple ascorbic acid is often the preferred source due to cost.",
